{"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time."}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Getting Started with Gnusto","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By the end of this guide you will have a game with two rooms, one object, one rule, and a test that plays it. It assumes you can write basic Swift; it assumes nothing about interactive fiction.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Prefer to start from something that already runs? ","type":"text"},{"code":"bin\/new-game Zwank ~\/dev\/Zwank","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes a complete starter package named for your game — then skim this guide for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}]},{"text":" behind each piece.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Add Gnusto to your package","anchor":"Add-Gnusto-to-your-package","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add Gnusto as a dependency, list it in your executable target, and give the test target the ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoTestSupport","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product (it links the toolchain’s Testing library, so it belongs in test targets only):","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ swift-tools-version: 6.2","import PackageDescription","","let package = Package(","    name: \"MyGame\",","    platforms: [.macOS(.v15)],","    dependencies: [","        .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/Gnusto\", from: \"0.1.0\")","    ],","    targets: [","        .executableTarget(","            name: \"MyGame\",","            dependencies: [","                .product(name: \"Gnusto\", package: \"Gnusto\")","            ]","        ),","        .testTarget(","            name: \"MyGameTests\",","            dependencies: [","                \"MyGame\",","                .product(name: \"GnustoTestSupport\", package: \"Gnusto\"),","            ]","        ),","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Gnusto needs a Swift 6.2 toolchain and the Swift 6 language mode. The ","type":"text"},{"code":".macOS(.v15)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" floor above is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Synchronization.Mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; Linux is tested in CI and needs no platform line. iOS is supported too, at ","type":"text"},{"code":".iOS(.v18)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the same reason. Add that line if your game is an app rather than a terminal program, and give it an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of its own — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomFrontEnds","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Declare a game","anchor":"Declare-a-game","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A game is a single type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"text":". Start with just a title and an intro:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import Gnusto","","struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" requires an "},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but Swift synthesizes it for free as long as every stored property has a default value — which they always will here, since rooms, items, and state are declared with initializers."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Add a room","type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-room"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a stored property. The property name ("},{"code":"hall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") becomes the room’s internal identity; the "},{"code":"name(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" trait is what the player sees."}]},{"code":["struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","","    let hall = Location {","        name(\"Entrance Hall\")","        description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","    }","","    var map: WorldMap {","        player.starts(in: hall)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block is where geography and starting positions live. "},{"code":"player.starts(in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" places the player; without it, the game has nowhere to begin."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Run it","type":"heading","anchor":"Run-it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two lines turn a game value into a running session:"}]},{"code":["let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" validates the game and builds its initial state up front — a mistake like an exit to an undeclared room is caught here, as a thrown "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", not at runtime. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs the prompt\/parse\/perform\/print loop, and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" reads from and writes to the terminal."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wrap it in a "},{"code":"do","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"catch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in your "},{"code":"main.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["import Gnusto","","do {","    let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","    await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()","} catch {","    print(\"Couldn't start the game: \\(error)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Run "},{"code":"swift run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and you can already "},{"code":"look","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" around and try to move."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Add a second room and connect them","type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-second-room-and-connect-them"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are declared on locations in the "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block. Each directional method ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", …) is an ordinary property reference, so a typo or a renamed room is a compile error, not a broken game."}]},{"code":["let hall = Location {","    name(\"Entrance Hall\")","    description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","}","","let library = Location {","    name(\"Dusty Library\")","    description(\"Shelves sag under mildewed books. The hall lies south.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are one-directional by design — declare both "},{"code":"hall.north(library)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"library.south(hall)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if you want the player to be able to walk back."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Add a thing","type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-thing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" the same way, then place it in the "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    adjectives(\"brass\", \"old\")","    description(\"An old brass lantern, its glass sooty but intact.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","    lantern.starts(in: library)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the player can walk "},{"code":"north","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"examine lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"take lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and see it in their "},{"code":"inventory","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" let them type "},{"code":"take brass lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"take old lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; a phrase has to end on a noun, so "},{"code":"take brass","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on its own is not one of them. The last word of "},{"code":"name(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (“lantern”) is the noun the parser keys on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything you declare is split into words the same way the parser splits what the player types — lowercased, a trailing possessive dropped, every other punctuation mark a separator. So "},{"code":"name(\"Mrs. Vane\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" prints its period and answers to "},{"code":"mrs vane","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"adjectives(\"master's\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same declaration as "},{"code":"adjectives(\"master\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Write the second: a declaration should read the way the parser stores it."}]},{"level":2,"text":"React with a rule","type":"heading","anchor":"React-with-a-rule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So far every verb uses its built-in behavior. To add your own logic, write a rule in the "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block. Rules are "},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hooks attached to a location, an item, or the whole world."}]},{"code":["var rules: Rules {","    lantern.after(.take) {","        say(\"It's heavier than it looks.\")","    }","","    library.before(.go) {","        guard command.direction != .south else { return }","        try refuse(\"There's no exit that way — only back south to the hall.\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The first rule runs ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the player successfully takes the lantern and adds a line of flavor with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)"},{"text":". The second runs ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"text":" movement in the library and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)"},{"text":"s any direction but south. Inside a rule body, bare identifiers like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"command"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player"},{"text":", and your own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lantern"},{"text":" refer to the live turn — reading and writing them touches the current game state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To learn what rules can do — the phases, the ordering, and the difference between ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refuse"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reply"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"say"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" — read "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Test it","type":"heading","anchor":"Test-it"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A play session is just typed input and printed output, so the natural test plays a scripted session and asserts on the transcript:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","struct MyGameTests {","    @Test func theLanternIsWhereTheBreezeSaysItIs() async throws {","        let transcript = try await play(MyGame(), [\"north\", \"take lantern\"])","        expectInOrder(transcript, [\"Dusty Library\", \"Taken.\"])","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"play"},{"type":"text","text":" boots the game and feeds it each command; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectInOrder"},{"type":"text","text":" asserts the beats appear in order and shows the full transcript when one doesn’t. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true},{"text":" for turn slicing and pinning the random stream.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"A fuller example","anchor":"A-fuller-example"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gnusto ships with "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cloak of Darkness"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", Roger Firth’s classic one-room demonstration game, as its ","type":"text"},{"code":"CloakOfDarkness","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target. It exercises nearly every feature in a page of code — dark rooms, a wearable cloak, scored actions, a losing state, and per-turn rules — and is worth reading start to finish once the basics click.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Next steps","anchor":"Next-steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"bin\/new-game","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the repo — writes the complete starter package this guide builds up to","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","isActive":true},{"text":" — how declarations, identity, and live references fit together","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true},{"text":" — exactly what happens each turn","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true},{"text":" — the full vocabulary of game logic","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true},{"text":" — teach the parser new words with ","type":"text"},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true},{"text":" — transcript tests with GnustoTestSupport","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","isActive":true},{"text":" — carry your own data on entities and in globals","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted"]}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Game":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A complete game: declarations, geography, and rules.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"title":"Game","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/game","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/south(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location\/south(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"south","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Location"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8MapEntryV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MapEntry"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An exit leading south to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"to"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"south(_:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AddingCustomVerbs":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Teach the parser words the built-in table doesn’t know."}],"title":"Adding Custom Verbs","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/addingcustomverbs","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameWorld":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gameworld","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameWorld"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameWorld"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The game world: owns all state, serializes all mutation, and runs the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"turn pipeline. The single ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a game sits between the REPL and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this actor.","type":"text"}],"title":"GameWorld"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/CustomStateAndTraits":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Carry your own data on entities and in globals, alongside the engine’s closed core.","type":"text"}],"title":"Custom State and Traits","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/customstateandtraits","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/BootstrapError":{"title":"BootstrapError","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BootstrapError","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"All problems with a game definition, reported at once."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BootstrapError","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/bootstraperror"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/north(_:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An exit leading north to "},{"code":"to","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location\/north(_:)","kind":"symbol","title":"north(_:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"north"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","text":"Location"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8MapEntryV","text":"MapEntry"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TestingYourGame":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/testingyourgame","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Play scripted sessions in your test suite and assert on the transcript.","type":"text"}],"title":"Testing Your Game"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/theturnpipeline","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","title":"The Turn Pipeline","abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/refuse(_:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refuse","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO","text":"Never","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Blocks the current action with a complaint. The default action and any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"remaining "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":" rules are skipped; world time still passes."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/refuse(_:)","title":"refuse(_:)"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/REPL":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/repl","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"REPL"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"REPL"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The outer loop: prompt → parse → perform → print, until the game ends or","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"input runs out. Holds the only ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a Gnusto game.","type":"text"}],"title":"REPL"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/IOHandler":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/iohandler","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IOHandler"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IOHandler"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Where the game’s text goes and player input comes from. Synchronous by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"design: a blocking console read is fine for a CLI; an async variant can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be added later without breaking this protocol’s clients.","type":"text"}],"title":"IOHandler"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/adjectives(_:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"adjectives","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"...) -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","text":"ItemTrait","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"adjectives(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Additional words the parser accepts before the item’s noun.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ConsoleIOHandler":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/consoleiohandler","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConsoleIOHandler"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConsoleIOHandler"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Plain terminal IO.","type":"text"}],"title":"ConsoleIOHandler"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"type":"topic","title":"Writing Rules","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A thing in the world."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Item","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/say(_:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"say","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Prints a message as part of the turn’s output."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/say(_:)","title":"say(_:)"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AnatomyOfAGame":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","title":"Anatomy of a Game","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A place in the world."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"title":"Location","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift."}],"title":"Gnusto","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/CustomFrontEnds":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomFrontEnds","abstract":[{"text":"Putting the engine behind something that is not a terminal.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/customfrontends","title":"Custom Front Ends"}}}